# Supply-chain hardening for the JavaScript side. See docs/build-log.md.
#
# 1. Direct dependencies are pinned exactly in web/package.json, but that alone
#    leaves transitive dependencies free to resolve to whatever was published
#    most recently — which is the exact window a compromised npm release
#    occupies. time-based resolution makes pnpm prefer transitive versions no
#    newer than the direct dependency that pulled them in, so the whole tree
#    stays inside the vetted window rather than just its top layer.
resolution-mode=time-based

# 2. Do not run dependency lifecycle scripts. The overwhelming majority of npm
#    compromises execute in a postinstall hook, so refusing to run them removes
#    the payload's delivery mechanism. Nothing in this stack needs one: the only
#    packages that wanted to build natively (bufferutil, utf-8-validate) are
#    optional accelerators for `ws` and fall back to pure JS.
ignore-scripts=true
